        <briefdescription>
<para>Loads a FBX file into memory and returns the loaded scene. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function loads an FBX file from the specified path, adjusting transforms if necessary. The target axes are left-handed with Y as up, and the target unit is set to be 0.01 meters. If the loading fails for any reason, it logs an error message and returns nullptr.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The file system path of the FBX file to load. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A pointer to the loaded ufbx_scene if successful, otherwise nullptr.</para>
</simplesect>
Loads an FBX file into a ufbx_scene object.</para>
<para>If the file cannot be loaded for any reason (e.g., it does not exist or is corrupt), an error message will be logged and nullptr will be returned. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
